WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:04.169
Bladesmiths, today's competition
revolves around barbarians,

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:07.407
specifically the Goths
who sacked Rome in 410 A.D.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.544
Along the way, the Goths seized
weapons of their adversaries

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.680
and incorporated them into
their own arsenals,

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.449
and today we're gonna ask you to
incorporate these weapons

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:21.454
into a billet from which
you will forge one of these.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.723
A favorite of backstabbers
everywhere.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.292
[suspenseful music playing]

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.695
A pugio dagger.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.997
<i> It is believed that the pugio</i>

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.066
<i> was the weapon used
 by the senate conspirators</i>

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:35.901
<i> to assassinate Julius Caesar</i>

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:38.571
<i>on the Ides of March in 44 A.D.</i>

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.307
Your challenge
in the first round

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.976 line:0%
<i> is to use a hada technique</i>

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.044 line:0%
<i> to combine three or more
 of these weapons</i>

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.345 line:0%
<i> to forge a pugio.</i>

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:49.515
Good luck, Bladesmiths.
Your three hours starts now.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:52.518
For my stack, I wanna have
nine pieces or more

00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:55.154
so that way, when you do
draw this out,

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.555
<i> you wanna make more metal
 than you need.</i>

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.225
<i> Having more is better
 than not having enough.</i>

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.294
[Alex]<i> Right now, I've got
 my billet welded up.</i>

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.229
I've got six separate pieces

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.164
<i> about four inches
 by an inch wide.</i>

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:06.633
<i> Got it tacked up, heating up.</i>

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.235
I've still got a few jitters
that I gotta work out,

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.538
but I think once I got
my billet set,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.405
I'm gonna be rollin'.

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:15.107
Double-edged daggers
I have no problem with.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.144
I've made 'em. But the challenge
of this weapon

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.680
<i> is the weapon
 has to be symmetrical.</i>

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.081
<i> You can't be off.</i>

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:23.582
The judges will see that.
They will know that.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.618
<i> If your measurement's wrong,
 you can go home.</i>

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:28.021
<i> Don't do your welds right,
 you can go home.</i>

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.555
I don't wanna go home.
I wanna be number one.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:32.158
[Kevin]<i> I start drawing
 the billet out lengthwise.</i>

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.461
<i> I don't wanna push out
 too much metal at one time.</i>

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.630
I want to maintain
that thickness of the blade

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.401
<i> because I know the judges
 are brutal when they test.</i>

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.069
Hot metal!

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.872
[bleep]! I don't know if I got
enough material.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:51.644
[Alex]<i> Every time you forge weld
 there's a chance of failure.</i>

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.347
So every time I forge weld,
I'm nervous.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.217
<i> My first forge weld
 is just a nice, light tap</i>

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.253
to make sure everything's set,
and then once I know

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.921
<i> that weld is set, I can start
 drawing this billet out.</i>

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:05.390
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:06.859
[Mike]
<i> When you're forge welding,</i>

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.094
<i> it's a repetitive process.</i>

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.064
<i> You have to heat, hammer,
 heat, hammer,</i>

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.466
so it becomes
one solid piece of metal.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:16.870
And when you're forge welding,
it's hit as hard as you can

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.471
<i> as fast as you can.</i>

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:24.043
[Ben] Alex did manage to do a
period correct Caesar quench.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.613
-Caesar quench?
-He stabbed that forge 23 times,

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.582
moving it in and out,
before he went to the oil.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.617
[Alex]<i> My knife's looking
 pretty straight.</i>

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:35.421
It sounds hard. Looks hard.
I'm feeling good.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.190
This is what I got so far.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.759
<i> I'm gonna go
 into the heat treat</i>

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.562
<i> and then do a little more
 finish grinding.</i>

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:46.666
Kevin just quenched his blade.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.968
-[David] File testing it.
-[Doug] Yeah.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.437
-That was quick.
-That was very fast.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.340
You gotta be [bleep]
kidding me.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.876
<i> Half of it's heat-treated,
 half of it's not.</i>

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.311
That is bad news.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:02.381
<i> On the second heat treat,
 I bring it up to cherry red.</i>

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:04.150
I got the same problem again.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.119
Kevin may be file checking
while it's still hot

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:08.521
and thinking it didn't get hard.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.990
So going for another quench
and then another quench.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.257
That makes sense.

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:15.094
[Kevin]<i> I'm starting to feel
 the pressure.</i>

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.729
<i> I know I gotta get
 on that grinder</i>

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.564
<i> to start getting
 this thing cleaned up.</i>

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.667
-And the tip looks very hot.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.234
[Wil] Come on, dude.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:25.605
[dramatic rock music playing]

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:26.772
[Kevin] Nope.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.806
What the hell's going on?

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:29.475
Don't know what I'm doing wrong.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.515
Oh, she's hard now.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.417
Phew. I'm good.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:42.154
The heat treat/quench
is what hardens your blade,

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:43.889
so when you're chopping
or cutting,

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:45.624
<i> it'll keep its edge.</i>

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.595
So I need it to be
fully hardened.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.030
Perfect.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:56.135
[Wil]
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.838
Shut down your machines!
Drop your tools!

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.172
Stop what you're doing!

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.908
This first round of
bladesmithing competition

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:04.777
is over!

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.412
Yeah, boys.

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:08.280
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.182
The old shield stab and chop.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.518
<i> To test the strength
 and durability</i>

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.286
<i> of your edges
 and points on your pugios,</i>

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.021
<i> as well as their
 overall construction,</i>

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:19.225
I'll be chopping and stabbing
mercilessly into theses shields.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.727
I don't really care what happens
to the shields.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.897
I want to see what happens
to your tip and your edges.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:26.331
Alex, you're up first. Ready?

00:04:26.431 --> 00:04:28.534
-Let's do it.
-All right.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.472 line:0%
[Alex]<i> I'm super nervous
 going into the testing.</i>

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.508 line:0%
<i> I'm not sure how my tang
 is gonna hold up</i>

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.076
after I just rewelded it.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.644
<i> My tip is thin,</i>

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.980
so I'm just really hoping
that it can hold up.

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:44.651
[dramatic music playing]

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:11.077
[tense music playing]

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:19.419
Well, Alex,
first things first...

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.987
you lost about a quarter inch
of your tip here.

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:25.391
I'm looking at the grain
in there and it's...

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.725
it's not as fine
as I'd like to see.

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:29.662
It's probably overheating
during the quenches.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:34.466
That aside, you left some
sharp corners of the wood

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.369
where the wood contacts
the brass

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:40.706
and it took a little nibble
outta my thumb right here.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.307
But, in total,

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:44.010
it's got a good classic
pugio shape

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.079
and your edge held up
really well.

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:50.616
-Kevin.
-Let's rock it, man.

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:52.685
[laughs] All right. Let's do it.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.822 line:0%
[Kevin]<i> I'm a little anxious</i>

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.357 line:0%
<i> to see how my knife's
 gonna perform.</i>

00:05:58.457 --> 00:05:59.658 line:0%
<i> One of two things
 are gonna happen.</i>

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:01.193
<i>Either that shield's gonna give</i>

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.595
or my blade's gonna snap.

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:07.033
[dramatic music playing]

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.389
All right, Kevin.
First things first...

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:31.524
your tip came off.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.227
This grain is bigger
than I like.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.428
You also lost a piece
of your edge right here.

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:37.930
There's a nibble out of it.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.199
We can go to your handle
construction here.

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.767
Don't call my baby ugly.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:42.801
No, sir.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.870
-[laughs]
-You were under a time crunch.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.840
You chose a method of completing
this challenge

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:50.675
in a way that's usable
and wieldable.

00:06:50.742 --> 00:06:52.511
-Well done.
-I'm down with it.

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.479
Mike, you're up next.
What're you thinking?

00:06:54.579 --> 00:06:56.783
-Let's do it.
-All right.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.020 line:0%
[Mike]<i> I haven't been nervous
 until right now,</i>

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.621 line:0%
<i> and I'm going crazy.</i>

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.189
<i> My competitors both
 lost their tips.</i>

00:07:04.256 --> 00:07:06.558
<i> If I can keep my tip, don't
 think I'ma have any problems.</i>

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:09.428
But this is outta my control.
This is in the judges' hands.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:12.799
[dramatic music playing]

00:07:26.878 --> 00:07:30.048
Mike, your blade
doesn't have medallions

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:31.584
on either side
of that handle,

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:34.653
and it is a critical feature
in a pugio.

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.956
Therefore, your blade
cannot be tested

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:39.458
<i> or measured evenly and fairly
 with your competitors',</i>

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:40.759
<i> and it doesn't make the cut.</i>

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.761
You did a lot of hard work
here, my friend,

00:07:42.861 --> 00:07:45.231
and it's an unfortunate
circumstance.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:48.901
At this time, I have to ask you
to please leave the Forge.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.302
Good job, guys.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:51.903
-Good job, guys.
-[whispering] Mike...

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.539
[Mike]<i> You're gonna
 come to this competition,</i>

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.908
make sure you pay attention
to the parameters.

00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:57.509
<i> It's very important.</i>

00:07:57.576 --> 00:08:00.680
The smallest detail
that you miss can get you off.

00:08:01.346 --> 00:08:02.681
<i>This was an amazing experience.</i>

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:05.551
I truly believe that if I had
my weapon tested,

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.186
I woulda went through
to the finals.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:10.289
What's next for me is go home,
probably make another pugio,

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.124
and I'ma send a picture
to the judges

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:13.726
<i>and say, "This is what I made."</i>

